sequenceDiagram
    actor User as CLI User
    participant picocli as picocli CommandLine
    participant SC as SetupCommand
    participant STS as AWS STS
    participant IAM as AWS IAM
    participant S3 as AWS S3
    participant DDB as AWS DynamoDB
    participant CFSvc as CloudFormationService
    participant CF as AWS CloudFormation
    participant FS as Local Filesystem

    Note over User,FS: baas admin deployment setup -- needs the elevated BaasCliDeployerPolicy.<br/>Deploys the CORE stack only. cf-template-ci.yaml is deployed by hand.
    User->>picocli: baas [--deployment D] admin deployment setup [--region] [--deployer-aws-profile]<br/>[--policy-file F] [--github-org --github-repo --oidc-provider-arn]
    picocli->>SC: parse and bind options into fields
    Note over SC: validate federation options before anything is loaded --<br/>a partial federation set -> exit 2. There are no networking options:<br/>every deployment uses the VPC its own stack creates
    SC->>FS: ConfigService.load()
    FS-->>SC: loadForSetup() -- deployments/D.yaml (or a new one named D), else the only one,<br/>else empty: the name is derived below. Two or more and no D: refused. D validated first, before any AWS call
    Note over SC: apply --region / --deployer-aws-profile over config defaults
    SC->>STS: sts.getCallerIdentity()
    STS-->>SC: account id
    Note over SC: prefix = D, the only configured one, else "baas-" + accountId<br/>stackName = bucketName = prefix<br/>tableName = prefix + "-results" (DeploymentNames)<br/>Nothing about the CALLER reaches the name -- a second<br/>deployment exists only because its name was typed.
    SC->>S3: BucketProbe -- headBucket(bucketName) here, then again in the region a redirect names
    Note over SC,S3: absent (404) / reachable in region X (200) / forbidden (403).<br/>From another region, ANY account's bucket answers 301 -- only its own<br/>region tells the caller's bucket (200) from another account's (403)
    alt reachable in ANOTHER region
        SC-->>User: the deployment lives there -- setup --region <it>, exit 1, no delete advice (U23)
    end
    Note over SC: BEFORE the preflight: a deployer's grants name one region, so elsewhere<br/>the preflight would print a policy inviting a second deployment
    Note over SC: render the deployer policy for this account, region and deployment
    opt --policy-file F
        SC->>FS: write F -- before the check, whatever it finds. Unwritable -> exit 1, nothing created
    end
    loop every action of every Allow statement without a Condition
        SC->>IAM: SimulatePrincipalPolicy(that action, its statement's resources as written)
    end
    Note over SC,IAM: opportunistic -- a caller that may not simulate gets no check.<br/>Judged on the action's overall decision (per-resource results flag type mismatches)
    alt denied
        SC-->>User: stderr names the denied actions and the IAM admin's commands<br/>(create-policy, attach, create-policy-version, BaasCliDeployerPolicy-prefix).<br/>STDOUT holds the policy (setup > policy.json still works) -- exit 1, nothing created
    end
    SC->>FS: load /templates/cf-template-core.yaml from the classpath
    FS-->>SC: template body

    SC->>CF: describeStacks(stackName) -- status?
    alt stack absent, or ROLLBACK_COMPLETE (create)
        SC->>DDB: describeTable(prefix-results) -- exists?
        alt bucket reachable HERE, bucket forbidden, or table exists
            SC-->>User: name the leftover and its removal (aws s3 rb / aws dynamodb delete-table),<br/>or for another account's bucket ask for another --deployment.<br/>Exit 1 -- nothing created, nothing deleted, a rolled-back stack left as it is (R16)
        end
        opt status ROLLBACK_COMPLETE
            Note over SC: a failed first create: no resources, no config file written
            SC->>CFSvc: deleteStack(stack) -- waits for DELETE_COMPLETE, then the create below (R1)
        end
    end
    alt stack exists and updatable (update)
        Note over SC: federation params carried forward unless named or revoked.
        Note over SC: image parameters: only those the deployed stack lacks.<br/>Base, parent and extension are carried forward, so a plain<br/>setup never reverts an image or drops an extension
        SC->>CFSvc: updateStackParameters(stack, template, changed params)
        CFSvc->>CF: updateStack(named params + UsePreviousValue for every other deployed<br/>param the template still declares -- an undeclared one would refuse the update)
        alt nothing changed
            CF-->>CFSvc: "No updates are to be performed" -- reported as already up to date
        else changes applied
            CFSvc->>CF: waiter.waitUntilStackUpdateComplete()
        end
    else create
        Note over SC: every image parameter is planned (parent resolved by<br/>DescribeImages in this region), never left at a template placeholder
        SC->>CFSvc: createStack(stack, template, explicit params incl. federation or empty)
        CFSvc->>CF: createStack(CAPABILITY_IAM, CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM)
        CFSvc->>CF: waiter.waitUntilStackCreateComplete()
    end
    opt the stack operation failed
        CFSvc->>CF: describeStackEvents -- the current operation's root-cause events
        alt a root cause is a denied permission
            SC-->>User: the events, the policy on STDOUT (or the --policy-file path)<br/>and the IAM admin's commands -- exit 1
        else any other cause
            SC-->>User: the events only -- exit 1
        end
    end

    SC->>CF: describeStacks() -- OperatorRoleArn output, to print only
    SC->>FS: ConfigService.save() -- deployments/<prefix>.yaml: aws.deployerProfile, resolved aws.region (the name is the file's)
    SC->>FS: write ~/.baas/runner-image-extension.yaml (beside deployments/, never in it), only if absent
    Note over SC,FS: nothing derivable or resolvable is stored

    alt created
        SC-->>User: BaasCliOperatorRole created -- your deployer credentials already operate it.<br/>A teammate: 1. grant sts:AssumeRole (see infra/README.md)<br/>2. baas --deployment <prefix> config sync --operator-aws-profile NAME<br/>Next: baas admin image build (~15 min)
    else updated
        SC-->>User: "Deployment <prefix> is deployed. Operator role: <arn>"
    end

    SC-->>User: exit 0
